{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There were shepherds out in the fields nearby
Keeping watch over their flock through the night
An angel of the [Gm]Lord [Eb]appeared to [Bb]them
And the [Gm]glory of the [Eb]Lord shone around [F]them
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sleep [Bb]now, little one, [Eb]sleep [Bb]now so softly
[Gm]A baby [Eb]wrapped in [F]cloths
[Bb]Sleep now, little [Eb]one, sleep [Bb]now so softly
[Gm]A baby [Eb]wrapped in [Bb]cloths
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Do not be afraid, [Eb]the angel told [Bb]them
I bring you good news [Eb]of great [Bb]joy
Today in the [Gm]city of David a Sav[Eb]ior is born to [Bb]you
He is [Gm]Christ the [F]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Sleep now, little [Eb]one, sleep [Bb]now so softly [Gm]
